# the panel manifest. verify_panel_provenance.py ships and reads it, and it is
# the only translation between a directory name like 05_I and the panel letter
# actually printed. 41 KB.
!03_Final_Panels/PROVENANCE.csv

# the printed geometry 00_Config/slots.py reads: one rect per printed panel, the
# sub-boxes of the panels that print several plots under one letter, each panel
# letter's size and box, and the three page sizes. 16 KB in total, measured off
# the published pages. Every script that asks for its printed size through
# slots.size_mm() raises FileNotFoundError without them, so an ignored copy
# would put the release back where it was before ship_slot_geometry() existed.
# Pure page coordinates in mm; no identifier and no expression value.
!03_Final_Panels/panel_rects.csv
!03_Final_Panels/slot_subrects.csv
!03_Final_Panels/letter_spec.csv
!03_Final_Panels/page_size.csv
!03_Final_Panels/panel_rects_v2.csv
!03_Final_Panels/slot_subrects_v2.csv
!03_Final_Panels/letter_spec_v2.csv
!03_Final_Panels/page_size_v2.csv

# the tables the drawing half of a panel reads (00_Config/cnsfig/cache.py,
# since 2026-09-15): per-sample means and group labels, neighbourhood positions,
# per-gene fold changes, dot-plot mean/fraction frames, GSEA running scores, UMAP
# positions with a cell-type label - and one MANIFEST.csv of md5s per directory.
# A panel script with its data/ table present redraws without opening an h5ad;
# without it the release could not redraw 2F, 2H/I, 2J, 3A/B/D/E, 4E, 5D/E, 5F,
# 5I, 1B or 1C from its own contents. Samples are named by study ID (P15-P1) or
# not at all; every file was scanned with scan_publish_safety.py. 13 MB, of which
# 7.3 MB is 1B's 238,931 UMAP positions.
!03_Final_Panels/01_Figure_1/01_B/data/MANIFEST.csv
